    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling offensive output today, anchored by the elite 82.13 projection for **Pete Crow-Armstrong**. Facing a favorable matchup against Ober and benefitting from a 5% boost due to favorable wind conditions, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** remains the primary target for stolen base production. His efficiency is further bolstered by Ober\u2019s slow delivery, which the model projects at an 87% success rate for SB attempts. **Christian Yelich** also earns a strong recommendation with a 72.74 score, leveraging a significant platoon advantage against Alcantara, S. Meanwhile, **Lars Nootbaar** projects as a sleeper play; while his base metrics are modest, the 5.29 xERA of Kelly, Me pushes his score to a 67.77, making him an excellent source of volume against a vulnerable starter.\n\nWe are forced to navigate a difficult matchup for **Casey Schmitt**, whose score of 42.15 keeps him in the starting lineup only by a narrow margin. He faces a formidable Miller, B (2.85 xERA), and while his dynamic platoon advantage provides a necessary floor, he is the most likely candidate to be pulled if we find ourselves near game cap limits. **Chase Meidroth** was the most difficult exclusion from today\u2019s roster; despite a respectable base projection, his lower-order placement (9th) and a sub-optimal matchup against Miles effectively lowered his score to 36.69, falling below the Zebras' 40-point threshold for mandatory starts. We continue to monitor the status of **Hyeseong Kim**, who remains in the minors, while **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** are held out due to team off-days. With **Dillon Dingler**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Yordan Alvarez**, **Junior Caminero**, and **Caleb Durbin** all clearing the 50-point barrier, the offense is well-balanced to chase volume in AVG and SB while maintaining a steady HR output.",
